            <ArticleTitle>Laparoscopic-assisted surgery for benign ovarian cyst in a young girl.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>295-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 7-year-old girl was admitted to our hospital because of sudden lower abdominal pain and vomiting. Emergency laparoscopy and cystectomy were performed, with a diagnosis of torsion of an ovarian cyst. All manipulations were possible through a 2-cm incision in the abdominal wall.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
